# The only credential this repo holds: the read-only Postgres role `console`,
# created by the pipeline repo's migration 0006 and given a password by hand on
# the box (../Fonnus/docs/runbook.md §9). Never the `fonnus` superuser.
#
# Local development through an SSH tunnel (see README.md):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://console:<password>@127.0.0.1:15432/fonnus
# On the box, as a container on the pipeline's network `fonnus_default`:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://console:<password>@postgres:5432/fonnus
DATABASE_URL=

# The second role, for the two inserts the contract allows (§7: a configuration
# edit, an annotation) — ADR 0007. Optional: unset, every screen reads as before
# and the edit surfaces say "editing not configured". Set, its username must be
# console_editor or the console refuses to start. Same two paths as DATABASE_URL;
# generated without a `$` (compose interpolates). Never the `fonnus` superuser.
# EDITOR_DATABASE_URL=postgres://console_editor:<password>@postgres:5432/fonnus

# The artifact bucket (../Fonnus PLAN row W2-L1, landed 2026-09-07; ADR 0019 there).
# One bucket holds every call's artifacts; endpoint and region are the ones the
# pipeline uses. The call detail page reads `call.wav` from here to play the
# recording (row A5, ADR 0004).
#
# All five keys or none: with none set, every recording surface says "recording
# access not configured"; with some but not all, the console refuses to start and
# names the missing keys, because a half-configured group is a typo and a typo
# must not degrade quietly into "not configured".
#
# Vietnix issues account-wide keys only: there is no per-bucket, read-only key to
# ask for. This repo therefore holds its OWN key pair (the `console` key), separate
# from the pipeline's `app` key and the developer `dev` key, so that each can be
# rotated alone — but any of them can write anywhere in the account. Consequence,
# accepted for this phase: the bucket holds internal test calls only for as long as
# such a key exists off the VPS (ADR 0019 decision 6).
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.vn-hcm-1.vietnix.cloud
# S3_REGION=vn-hcm-1
# S3_BUCKET=recordinginternal
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# The consent gate (ADR 0005) — `on` or `off`, and nothing else; any other value
# refuses to start, so a misspelling cannot land on either side by accident.
#
# `on` is the default and applies when the key is unset: caller text and the
# recording are withheld unless the call's consent outcome is `granted`. `off` is
# set only in the internal test deployment's .env, where every caller is a team
# member who consented off-band and the calls whose disclosure needs tuning are
# exactly the ones with no grant on record. When it is off, every screen says so.
# CONSENT_GATE=on

# Deployment on the box only (docs/deploy.md); nothing under src/ reads these.
#
# ADMIN_DOMAIN is read by compose, not by the app: the hostname Caddy serves and
# requests a Let's Encrypt certificate for. Its A record must resolve BEFORE Caddy
# first starts — failed validations are rate-limited. On the box it is
# admin.fonnus.me.
ADMIN_DOMAIN=
# The image ops/deploy.sh pulls and prunes. The tag is passed per deploy
# (ADMIN_IMAGE_TAG), never stored here.
# ADMIN_IMAGE=ghcr.io/voidkeishi/fonnus-admin
#
# Compose parses this file, so a `$` in a value is interpolation ($$ escapes it).
# The `console` password is generated without one: `openssl rand -hex 24`.
